CONTRIBUTIONS IN THIS REPOSITORY
--------------------------------

Bug fixes to the upstream project:

  1. Replaced a decommissioned Groq model. The project pinned
     `llama-3.1-8b-instant`, which Groq has since retired; every model
     evaluation crashed with a 404.

  2. Bounded LLM output tokens. No `max_tokens` was set on any completion
     call, so Groq's free tier rejected requests outright (it estimates a
     request's output up front: an estimated 1168 tokens against a 1000
     tokens/minute ceiling). Fixed at all four call sites.

  3. Fixed a silently broken model-promotion quality gate. The promotion
     logic read the metric key `answer_correctness/v1/mean`, which only
     MLflow's built-in judge emits; a custom metric emits
     `answer_correctness/mean`. The score therefore read as None, defaulted
     to 0.0 for every candidate, and the "best" model was selected on
     coherence and latency alone. Fixing it changed the actual outcome of a
     promotion round.

  4. Enabled unbuffered container logging. Without PYTHONUNBUFFERED, every
     print() from the startup automation was buffered and invisible, making
     startup failures look like silence.

  5. Corrected documentation left stale by the above changes.

New functionality:

  6. A "lite" Docker Compose profile. The upstream stack requires ~16GB of
     RAM for Docker alone, largely due to OpenMetadata (~5GB across four
     containers). Gating those behind a Compose profile brings the stack to
     ~2.2GB measured, so it runs on an ordinary 16GB laptop.

  7. A local column-tag source for the data-governance layer, so Layer 3
     still makes a real OPA masking decision when OpenMetadata is not
     deployed. The tag SOURCE changes between profiles; the policy
     evaluation does not.

  8. A configurable fail-open/fail-closed mode for the data layer
     (DATA_LAYER_FAIL_MODE). Upstream silently served unmasked data when the
     catalog was unreachable; an unreachable catalog is not evidence that a
     column is safe.

  9. A MODEL_PROFILE switch selecting between an all-Groq provider set
     (free tier, no OpenAI credit required) and the original two-provider
     set, including a provider-agnostic LLM judge, since MLflow's genai
     metrics support no "groq:/" URI scheme.

 10. The project's first Python test suite, including a drift test that
     fails if the two tag sources ever disagree about which columns are PII.

 11. Continuous integration, dependency auditing, container hardening, and
     the documentation under docs/.

 12. Extracted the Layer 3 tag/masking logic into agent/data_tags.py, which
     depends only on PyYAML. Previously this logic could only be imported
     alongside mlflow, guardrails and agent_os, so CI could not exercise it
     without installing the entire runtime — the test suite skipped silently
     and reported a green build that had verified nothing.

Documented (not fixed) upstream issue:

 13. The SPIRE agent attests with a single-use join token and therefore
     shuts down when its SVID expires, taking the agent with it. Recovery
     steps and the proper fix are written up in RUNNING.md.
